    {
      "id": "05e585c6-4338-50ba-9019-48c5944052ec",
      "name": "Note 2ac9982c",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Flow: lessons\nEvery minute: save **Flow config** to the database \u2192 claim up to 200 due rows \u2192 Gate \u2192 one lane per step (top to bottom, in order); Send advances the row; an exit leaves a private note on the conversation. Marketers edit only the yellow nodes and publish. **Flow config**: `inbox_id` is the Chatwoot inbox (channel) the texts go out on; `status` is `paused` until you set it to `active` (paused: no enrollments, no sends); `reentry_policy` never / after_completion / after_exit / always; `holidays` are dates like \"2026-12-25\"; `flow_window_open`/`close` (\"10:00\"/\"18:00\", contact-local) are optional; `rep_first_name`, `rep_phone` and `checkout_url` fill the matching placeholders (the enroll webhook can send a per-contact `checkout_url`). **Step config**: message, delay_to_next, delay_unit. `{{first_name}}`, `{{name}}`, `{{rep_first_name}}`, `{{rep_phone}}`, `{{checkout_url}}` and any contact attribute key are placeholders. Never connect one lane to another.",
        "width": 1400,
        "height": 210,
        "color": 1
      }
    },
